# C3 substrate hardening fragment — vps-kvm ONLY. Merged AFTER kernel-hardening.config by
# build-kernel.sh (KernelInputs.substrate_fragment when substrate == VpsKvm). Force-DISABLES the USB
# HOST/STORAGE stack the linux-virt base ships (USB=m, promoted to builtin by MODULES=n):
# a KVM/hypervisor VPS boots off its VIRTUAL DISK, never off USB media, so the USB stack is dead attack
# surface. Disabling the USB parent cascades every USB-gated host-controller + mass-storage driver
# off. USB_PCI, however, is `default y, depends on PCI` — NOT gated on USB — so it survives
# the parent disable and, via its host/pci-quirks.o Makefile object (keyed on USB_PCI), would compile live PCI-fixup
# code (a DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_CLASS_FINAL BIOS-handoff quirk that runs at boot against USB-class PCI
# devices). It is force-DISABLED explicitly too so the USB shed is COMPLETE, not just the /dev-node drivers
# (audit F-1). USB_PCI_AMD (`depends on USB_PCI`) then cascades off with it.
#
# SCOPE (deliberately USB-only): the box's DISK transport varies by hypervisor — virtio-blk (Infomaniak),
# virtio-scsi, NVMe, or emulated SATA/AHCI — so the base's SCSI/ATA/NVMe/BLK_DEV_SD stack STAYS enabled
# (and is PINNED in the shared block, audit L-1) and the box boots on ANY KVM VPS. Shedding those (an
# earlier, over-eager design) would silently lock fruit-basket to virtio-blk hosts. USB is the one class a
# VPS genuinely never needs (bare-metal-uefi, which boots off USB media, ENABLES it via
# kernel-hardening-baremetal.config). The vps-kvm forbidden_prefix guard on the USB domain then
# FAIL-CLOSES on any USB `=y` driver, current or future, that isn't on the small inert-flag allowlist.
#
# --- the USB host/storage stack (a vps-kvm guest never boots off USB media) ---
# Disabling the USB parent alone cascades the USB-gated children off; the host-controller + storage
# lines are listed explicitly too so the fragment↔forbidden fast test verifies each, and intent is legible.
# CONFIG_USB is not set
# CONFIG_USB_XHCI_HCD is not set
# CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD is not set
# CONFIG_USB_STORAGE is not set
# CONFIG_USB_PCI is not set
